      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yup, had that happening to me since the first beta as well with the strings on my hoodie. Getting down to why this was happening is kinda diffecult as you said.\nHere are also two older canny about this from me:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-dynamics-reports-and-feedback/p/1184-small-max-stretch-doesnt-work-with-stretch-parameter\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-dynamics-reports-and-feedback/p/1186-phys-bone-paramters-wont-work-correctly-in-some-weird-situations",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-16T21:53:50.943Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If you export .fbx from blender with the default scale setting of Local, it causes your Armature transform to be scaled by 100.\nIn the SDK, PhysBone mostly works fine with scale 100, except that if you have a bone with a small max-stretch, for example 0.2, the _Stretch parameter stays 0. If you make stretch bigger, like 2 or 3, then the _Stretch parameter works... but it is stretched way too much.\nExporting with FBX All makes the armature scale 1,1,1 which allows the _Stretch parameter to work properly even at small stretch values such as 0.2.\nThe debugging process that went into narrowing this down was quite difficult.",
